    "body": "### Problem\n\nIf the `nvim.multicursor` namespace is cleared in insert mode, this will also clear any pending 'live' edits created by the multicursors. The edit created by the primary cursor is preserved.\n\nRelated(?): #42205\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n``` lua\n-- minimal.lua\n\nvim.keymap.set(\"i\", \"<c-l>\", function()\n    local mc_ns = vim.api.nvim_create_namespace('nvim.multicursor')\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_clear_namespace(0, mc_ns, 0, -1)\nend, {})\n```\n\n1. `nvim --clean -u minimal.lua`\n2.  Add the following to a blank buffer:\n    ```\n    foo\n    bar\n    ```\n3.  Type `vipQ` to place a multicursor at the start of each line\n4.  Type `iprefix <c-l><esc>` to insert `\"prefix \"` at the start of each line, clear mcursors, and exit insert mode\n5.  The final file looks like this:\n    ```\n    foo\n    prefix bar\n    ```\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nMulticursor edits should not disappear after clearing the `nvim.multicursor` namespace.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1943+gd714648b8e\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 26.6.2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nBuild from main",
